From 0b4e05b88419ffee0cdecc81203e6579052b6dd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TEX8 Wallet Engineering <wallet@tex8.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:57:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wallet: spill public BlockStream overflow to bounded disk

Keep the existing one-chunk per-lane RAM hot buffer. When it is full,
persist only public, validated BlockStream payloads to an app-private,
bounded disk spool and consume them in the original queue order. This lets
the six transport lanes continue while the unchanged wallet scanner works.

Every spilled payload is written mode 0600, flushed, CRC-checked on read,
deleted immediately after consumption, and removed on close. Missing, full,
or failing spool storage falls back to the established bounded RAM
backpressure path. Process-wide counters expose aggregate transport and
spool state without any wallet identifiers or private material.
---
